    "name": "PhoSim",
    "description": "PhoSim is a set of extremely fast photon Monte Carlo codes that calculate the ab initio physics of the atmosphere and a telescope & camera in order to simulate realistic optical/UV/IR/X-ray astronomical images.  PhoSim can also simulate any optical system that produces images (e.g. cameras, satellites, human eye).",
